implementationPlan.description:
The fix: three hunks, each kept clear of the peer rows' hunks in the same files. task-37e03b91 edits Models.kt around 91-120, MoeJson.kt around 24 and 604-630, and TaskDetailDialog.kt around 452-467. task-40813cc1 edits ProjectSettings (Models.kt:47+) and parseProjectSettings (MoeJson.kt:278+).
(a) Models.kt:124-132 HandoffNote: replace `val from: String? = null, val to: String? = null, val createdAt: String? = null,` with `val releasedBy: String? = null, val releasedAt: String? = null, val reason: String? = null,`. Keep them nullable with null defaults; the four body fields are unchanged. Add a one-line KDoc above the class: it is a release_task hand-off note, keyed as the daemon writes it (HandoffNote in packages/moe-daemon/src/types/schema.ts). DELETE from/to/createdAt outright rather than keeping them alongside:
  - the daemon has never written them (HandoffNote has had releasedBy/releasedAt/reason since 480dd8a9, 2026-05-15);
  - all 18 notes on the live board carry releasedBy/releasedAt/reason and none carry from/to/createdAt, so dropping them is backward-compatible with existing .moe/ state;
  - with them gone, any leftover read is a compile error.
  Nothing else reads them: TaskCard.kt:155 uses only priorHandoffs.size, and nothing re-serializes the note.
(b) MoeJson.kt:512-528 parseHandoffs: read `releasedBy`, `releasedAt` and `reason` with getStringOrNull, in place of from, to and createdAt. Error handling stays exactly as lenient as today:
  - getStringOrNull returns null for a missing, null or non-primitive value (MoeJson.kt:44-52);
  - a non-object entry is skipped;
  - a non-array priorHandoffs yields null.
  So a note without the keys parses to nulls and never throws.
(c) TaskDetailDialog.kt:910-918 handoffBlocks: the header buildString becomes
  append("#").append(i + 1)
  if (!h.releasedBy.isNullOrBlank()) append(" released by ").append(h.releasedBy)
  if (!h.releasedAt.isNullOrBlank()) append(" (").append(h.releasedAt).append(")")
  if (!h.reason.isNullOrBlank()) append(": ").append(h.reason)
  The pieces are independent, like the old code, so a note with none of them renders "#N".
  The reason is free text, capped at 2000 chars by releaseTask.ts:241/294. Swing's TitledBorder constrains its title label to the panel width, so a long reason ends in "...". No truncation, whitespace folding or tooltip is added: 0 of the 18 live reasons contain a line break.
  Leave HandoffBlock, the Swing loop at :616-637 and MoeBundle.properties (held by task-37e03b91) untouched. The literal " released by " mirrors the old literal " from ": the companion is pure and headless, with no bundle lookups.
